      "check": "naproxen_source_scope_is_narrow",
      "ok": true,
      "detail": "For this local queue, a medication-category aspirin AllergyIntolerance with no documented reaction phenotype is not cleared by an informal 'no drug allergy documented' line on a later specialty note. Current naproxen labeling specifically warns about aspirin-sensitive asthma and cross-reactivity; it does not establish that every generic aspirin-allergy entry has that phenotype. Under the conservative local workflow, when the allergy remains uncharacterized and no allergist exception is on file, do not label or dispense the refill. Place the request in pending-allergy-review, notify the prescriber, and do not discontinue the osteoarthritis plan. Current naproxen labeling: https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2024/017581s117%2C018164s067%2C020067s026lbl.pdf. If the governing inputs require a hold, apply it at scenario://ehr/pharmacy/RXQ-CAL21/pending-allergy-review."
